  "settings":{"anchor":"about","eyebrow":"what cuesea is","head_a":"your systems know everything.","head_b":"the room knows nothing.","col_one":"<p>every business already has the sea: point of sale, ecommerce, loyalty, service tickets, work orders, reservations, warranty history. the coat she almost bought in march. the compressor that failed twice last winter.</p>","col_two":"<p>it sits in systems the person doing the work cannot open, in dashboards nobody reads standing up, in reports that arrive on tuesday about a saturday. cuesea reads them where they already are and delivers one sentence into the line of sight of whoever is in the room — an associate, a host, a technician, a rep. one sentence they can say out loud exactly as written.</p>"}},

"surfaces": {"type":"surfaces","blocks":{
  "u1":{"type":"surface","settings":{"tag":"in the glass · even g2","lead":true,"title":"cue lens","body":"576 × 288, monochrome, every row the same size because 26px is the legibility floor on that display. sideloads through even hub. ring and temple for gestures, and a double press opens the mic — the answer is in the glass in about three seconds."}},
  "u2":{"type":"surface","settings":{"tag":"in the glass · meta ray-ban display","lead":false,"title":"cue lens","body":"600 × 600 in colour, running on the glasses themselves as a web app rather than through a phone bridge. the neural band and captouch drive it. no microphone on that path, so this surface reads rather than listens. built against the same core and running today in a browser — not yet in a store."}},
  "u3":{"type":"surface","settings":{"tag":"in the hand · no glasses needed","lead":true,"title":"cue pocket","body":"an installable web app running the same card deck from the same core. a thumb makes the same six gestures a neural band does, so nothing below the input layer knows which surface it is on. it works on a dead network, and it never writes a guest to the handset."}}},
  "block_order":["u1","u2","u3"],
  "settings":{"anchor":"surfaces","eyebrow":"one cue, three surfaces","title":"the sentence is written once","standfirst":"composed under the hardest constraint there is — three lines in a monochrome lens — and then rendered wherever the person actually is.","footnote":"a pilot does not need glasses in the building: pocket is the same product on a phone the associate already owns, which is what makes “no hardware to start” a fact rather than a slogan. the meta build is real code rather than a roadmap slide, and it is marked as what it is."}},

