  "settings":{"anchor":"ask","eyebrow":"the ask","title":"press once. ask out loud.","lede":"a double press opens the mic. the endpointer closes it when you stop talking rather than running to a cap — so the answer arrives in about three seconds, in the same glass, without a phone coming out.","intents":"stock, location, price, history, recommend, open","body":"<p>six intents, detected from the transcript. inventory by size with the nearest available sizes in the same sizing scheme, floor location, price, the guest's own record — their sizes, their open cart, their points and tier, what they have bought before — and recommendations matched against what is actually on the floor, excluding what they already own.</p><p>“do you have these in a 32” resolves “these” to whatever is on the lens at that moment.</p>","honest":"naming a garment the floor does not carry gets “we don't carry that”, not a confident answer about something else. answers are grounded in records we hold; the model is forbidden from estimating stock, sizes or prices, and an outage says “model unavailable” rather than guessing."}},

"floor": {"type":"capability","blocks":{
  "p1":{"type":"point","settings":{"title":"addressed, not broadcast","body":"a message with nobody's name on it is the floor radio, as before. put a name on it and it reaches one person's lens and nobody else's, marked “→ you” so it can never be mistaken for the room. reply, and the reply goes back to that person rather than to the floor."}},
  "p2":{"type":"point","settings":{"title":"urgent takes the frame. everything else waits.","body":"anything not marked urgent queues behind an unread marker on the rail, because a message that interrupts a customer conversation had better have earned it."}},
  "p3":{"type":"point","settings":{"title":"off means off","body":"a retailer can turn floor messages off, and the server refuses delivery rather than merely hiding the composer. it is a switch, not a suggestion."}}},
  "block_order":["p1","p2","p3"],
  "settings":{"anchor":"floor","eyebrow":"the floor","title":"one channel, with a name on it","lede":"a radio that only ever shouts at everybody is a radio people stop hearing. so a cue can be sent to one person.","cue":"BRING A 32 TO FIT 3\nFROM TOM R\nUNREAD 1","name":"AMARA K","facts":"FLOOR,DENIM,UNREAD 1","rail":true,"zone":"DENIM WALL","meta":"DM · NOW","clock":"14·32","caption":"an addressed message, on the rail rather than in the way","footnote":"canned phrases send from the ring without stopping what you are doing. free text is typed on pocket's floor card or dictated in studio."}},

"look": {"type":"capability","blocks":{
  "q1":{"type":"point","settings":{"title":"barcodes are decoded, never guessed","body":"when the capture contains a barcode the code comes from a decoder, and the model is not consulted at all. the model is the fallback for what a decoder cannot read — a washed-out swing tag, a handwritten style number, a care label."}},
  "q2":{"type":"point","settings":{"title":"objects. never people.","body":"there is no face detection and no person matching on this path, and there is no version of it that quietly becomes one. a photograph whose subject is a person comes back refused, and the refusal is the answer in the glass."}},
  "q3":{"type":"point","settings":{"title":"the image is never stored","body":"not to disk, not to the database, not to a log line, not to an analytics row. bytes in, strings out, gone with the request."}}},
  "block_order":["q1","q2","q3"],
  "settings":{"anchor":"look","eyebrow":"the look-up","title":"point the phone at the tag","lede":"the glasses have no camera, and that is a decision rather than a gap. the phone already in the associate's pocket does — so a swing tag, a barcode or a snapped bracket becomes an answer in the glass.","cue":"HALDEN STRAIGHT 32\n2 ON THE DENIM WALL\nNONE IN THE BACK","name":"SCAN","facts":"SKU,EAN 13,ON FLOOR,2 LEFT","rail":true,"zone":"DENIM WALL","meta":"LOOK · 1.8S","clock":"14·36","caption":"what comes back from a tag, in the same three lines","footnote":"the pilot store's variants carried no barcodes at all, so cuesea derives a valid in-store ean-13 for each one from its sku. the same sku always yields the same barcode, so reprinting a label never churns it."}},

